@.str.171 = private unnamed_addr constant [917 x i8] c"\0A          Allow this store to be opened when its [database](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-nix-database) is on a read-only filesystem.\0A\0A          Normally Nix will attempt to open the store database in read-write mode, even for querying (when write access is not needed), causing it to fail if the database is on a read-only filesystem.\0A\0A          Enable read-only mode to disable locking and open the SQLite database with the [`immutable` parameter](https://www.sqlite.org/c3ref/open.html) set.\0A\0A          > **Warning**\0A          > Do not use this unless the filesystem is read-only.\0A          >\0A          > Using it when the filesystem is writable can cause incorrect query results or corruption errors if the database is changed by another process.\0A          > While the filesystem the database resides on might appear to be read-only, consider whether another user or system might have write access to it.\0A        \00", align 1
